    "titleText": {
      "es": "No, sí que tenemos una mujer que básicamente forma parte de nuestra comunidad. Vive en Rivendel, no creo que la conozcas.",
      "en": "No, we actually do have a woman who's basically part of our fellowship. She lives in Rivendell, you wouldn't know her.",
      "noteEn": "The Spanish title and title text are preserved exactly from the Spanish archive, while the English fields reproduce official xkcd #2609. In the raster, each printed ENT-MUJERES is split at its visible hyphen: ENT is the untranslated fictional species name and is inventoried as non-Spanish text, while MUJERES remains a Spanish lexical occurrence. SAURON is likewise inventoried as a proper-name exclusion."
