    {
      "id": "grammar-ordinal-before-noun-agreement",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "número ordinal antes de un sustantivo",
      "questionEn": "How do you use words such as first, second, or third before a Spanish noun?",
      "answerEn": "Put the ordinal before the noun and make its ending match the noun's gender and number.",
      "noteEn": "An ordinal gives a position in an order. Primero, segundo, tercero, último, and similar words usually come before the noun. Most forms use -o with a masculine singular noun and -a with a feminine singular noun, but primero and tercero shorten to primer and tercer before a masculine singular noun. Plural nouns use plural forms.",
      "example": {
        "es": "La segunda puerta está en el tercer piso.",
        "en": "The second door is on the third floor."
      },
      "tags": [
        "grammar",
        "ordinals",
